# GitHub PR / issue comments

## Gate

Comment **only** when the user asks to comment, reply, leave a review note, or
post a status update on a named PR/issue. Ordinary coding does not authorize
drive-by comments.

Never invent owner/repo or issue/PR number.

## Prefer MCP

When a GitHub MCP is ready:

- Issue / PR conversation: `add_issue_comment` (PR number works as issue
  number)
- Review comments on a pending review: `add_comment_to_pending_review` /
  `pull_request_review_write`
- Replies: `add_reply_to_pull_request_comment`

Do not use `gh` for the same comment while MCP works (`global-mcp-first`).

## Comment craft

- Short, operator-facing prose. Lead with the outcome or ask.
- Evidence-backed: cite check name, file path, or SHA when relevant.
- No secrets, tokens, private personal data, or unredacted production
  payloads.
- No paste of entire CI logs — link or quote a tight failure line.
- Do not @-spam or request reviews unless the user asked.
- Review bodies: prefer actionable findings over style nit floods. Match
  `code-reviewer` severity when the comment is a review.

## Reviews vs chat comments

| Intent | Path |
| --- | --- |
| Conversational update on the PR | Issue comment |
| Line-level review finding | Pending review comment → submit review |
| Approve / request changes | Only when the user explicitly asks for that event |

## Done

Return the comment URL or confirm the review was submitted. Stop — do not
implement product code unless the user added an explicit implement verb.
